---
title: American Pancakes
servings: 4
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 20 minutes
difficulty: easy
cuisine: american
protein: egg
course: dessert
tags:
  - quick
  - weekday
  - kid-friendly
  - mild
equipment:
  - large mixing bowl
  - mixing bowl
  - whisk
  - non-stick frying pan
---

Sift @plain flour{135%g}, @baking powder{1%tsp}, @salt{1/2%tsp}, and @caster sugar{2%tbsp} into a #large mixing bowl{}.

In a separate #mixing bowl{} or jug, lightly whisk @milk{130%ml} with @egg{1%piece}, then whisk in @butter{2%tbsp}(melted and cooled slightly, plus extra for cooking and serving).

Pour the milk mixture into the flour mixture and beat with a #whisk{} or fork until you have a smooth, thick batter. Let the batter stand for a few minutes.

Heat a #non-stick frying pan{} over medium heat and add a small knob of butter. When melted, add a ladleful of batter, or two if the pan is large enough.

Cook for about ~{3%minutes}, until the top begins to bubble and the edges start to set. Flip and cook for another ~{2%minutes}, until both sides are golden brown and the pancake has risen to about 1 cm thick. If the pancake darkens too much, reduce the heat slightly for the next one.

Repeat with the remaining batter, adding more butter to the pan as needed. Keep cooked pancakes warm in a low #oven{} if needed, though they are best fresh from the pan.

Serve with @maple syrup{} and extra butter.
